& [Delineation]
  + READY stopped means procedure state is nonterminal exact and resumable through the returned registry and handle
  + terminal awaiting reflection means procedure state is complete but provider reflection is absent and is not a READY stop
  + provider protocol refusal before advancement leaves the previous READY registry unchanged
  + tool-cap exhaustion after advancement retains the new READY registry and admitted iteration
  + missing scripted response is absence evidence while invalid scripted response is retained sanitized failure evidence

& [SelectedForms]
  + ScriptedStoppedRun contains only a stopped IterativeReport and exact live READY successor registry
  + failed request exists only for provider-protocol stop and is reconstructed from the admitted prefix
  + sanitized failed response is optional because script exhaustion supplies no response
  + provider call usage increments for a supplied invalid envelope but not for a missing envelope
  + tool usage increments only after provider response and deterministic advancement jointly admit one IterationRecord
  + resume helper reconstructs BoundSession only after full wrapper validation

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty keeps complete terminal READY stopped missing response and invalid response claims distinct
  + Security proves reentry handle by exact final registry INSPECT
  + Planner enforces exact cap usage and finite response consumption
  + Weaver replays all admitted iterations and reconstructs the failed next request
  + Scribe retains sanitized failure evidence and reason without private reasoning
  + Refiner omits failed response when none existed and omits all terminal fields
  + Observer admits only a READY head with reentry true and mutually consistent report wrapper and registry

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated scripted_stopped forms runner validator resume helper fixtures and focused tests
  + retain terminal-reflection-pending transport process clock persistence and all external effects under separate locks

& [Rollback]
  + additive module exports and tests remove without changing predecessor behavior or stored data
